@startuml qnx_dispatch_engine_lifecycle_activity
title QnxDispatchEngine - object lifetime

start
if (Entry is construction?) then (yes)
    :Retain borrowed memory resource, move OSAL adapters and logger,\nconstruct both runners, empty endpoint storage and timer queue;
    :SetupResourceManagerCallbacks()\ninitializes connect/io tables and installs native callbacks;
    :client_runner_.Start with InitClientThread();
    note right
        InitClientThread runs in the constructing thread
        under the client runner mutex.
        Attach timer, select and connection-death pulses;
        create a CLOCK_MONOTONIC pulse timer.
        Checked initialization failures log and terminate.
    end note
    :server_runner_.Start with InitServerThread();
    note right
        InitServerThread runs in the constructing thread
        under the server runner mutex.
        Set up resource-manager dispatch buffering
        with a null-path resmgr_attach.
        StartPostInit then allocates the server dispatch
        context and its receive workspace.
        A checked failure logs and terminates.
    end note
    :Return with separate client and server dispatch threads;
    stop
else (destruction)
    :server_runner_.Stop();
endif

if (Client dispatch pointer is non-null?) then (yes)
    :Destroy timer_id_ through TimerDestroy()\nwithout checking the result;
    :client_runner_.Stop();
else (not initialized)
    :Skip client timer and runner teardown;
endif
:Destroy remaining members after the explicit joins;
stop

legend
    Runner startup and stopping are separate procedures.
    Destruction stops the server before destroying the client timer
    and stopping the client. This order does not establish a finite
    shutdown deadline or qualify destruction from a callback thread.
endlegend

@enduml
